    "/documents/from-url": {
      "post": {
        "description": "Ingest the posting published at an address (FR-1).\n\nThe third way into the same knowledge base, after a paste and a file, and\nit answers exactly like them: 201 for a new posting, 200 with the\nexisting one for a duplicate, the same DocumentRead either way. Nothing\nbelow _store knows the text arrived over the network.\n\nWhich addresses are read is settled by the allowlist rather than here --\nsee NFR-5 for why the list is closed, and app.services.scraping for the\nrequest forgery it also prevents (NFR-1).\n\nParsing runs on the event loop rather than in a worker thread, which is\nthe opposite of what the upload route does with a PDF. The measurement is\nthe reason: a megabyte of markup takes about ten milliseconds here,\nbecause HTMLParser skips script bodies wholesale, while a PDF of the same\nsize takes hundreds. Below a certain cost the hand-off is the expensive\npart.\n\nThe fetch happens inside the trace, not before it, so a board that took\neight seconds to answer is visible as what made the ingestion slow\n(NFR-2). It costs no money, which is why the rate limit it shares with\nthe other two routes is still about embeddings.",
        "operationId": "ingest_from_url_documents_from_url_post",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/DocumentFromUrl"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/DocumentRead"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "security": [
          {
            "HTTPBearer": []
          }
        ],
        "summary": "Ingest From Url",
        "tags": [
          "documents"
        ]
      }
    },
    "/documents/upload": {
      "post": {
        "description": "Ingest a source from an uploaded PDF, DOCX or text file (FR-1).\n\nThe same knowledge base as the JSON route, reached with a file instead\nof a paste, and answering the same way: 201 for a new source, 200 with\nthe existing one for a duplicate.\n\nNo file hash is stored, and that is the point. A document is identified\nby the hash of its normalised text, so the same posting sent once as a\nPDF and once as a DOCX is correctly one document -- two different files,\none source. Hashing the bytes here would break that, which is the\nopposite of what it does for resumes, where the hash is what makes a\nre-upload recognisable.\n\nThe fields are declared one by one rather than as a single Form model:\nFastAPI flattens such a model only when every field is scalar, and\nmetadata is an object, so the whole thing arrives as one missing field.\nThey are validated together anyway, by handing them to DocumentUpload --\na real URL and metadata that parses -- so the two routes reject the same\ninput for the same reasons.\n\nThe length limit the JSON route gets from its schema is applied by hand:\na 5 MB file of prose parses to far more text than MAX_CONTENT_LENGTH\nallows, and nothing would otherwise stop it.\n\nThe title falls back to the filename, which is the only name an upload\ncomes with and better than nothing in a listing.",
        "operationId": "upload_document_documents_upload_post",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "multipart/form-data": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Body_upload_document_documents_upload_post"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/DocumentRead"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "security": [
          {
            "HTTPBearer": []
          }
        ],
        "summary": "Upload Document",
        "tags": [
          "documents"
        ]
      }
    },
